WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.534
-Guys, before we start,
just a reminder,

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.437
this is like a meeting between
Trump and his lawyer.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.739
It is all being recorded.
So, just so you know.

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:08.708
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.743
That's right.
Did you guys hear about this?

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.478
Last night,
CNN released a recording

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:14.948
of Trump and his lawyer
talking about using hush money

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:18.384
to cover up his affair with
Playboy model Karen McDougal.

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:20.286
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.054
In response, Trump was like,

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:24.790
"Oh, no, Stormy Daniels might
find out I cheated on her.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.559
Oh, no.
What I'm gonna do?"

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:29.963
[ Applause ]

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:32.198
That's right.
The tape is from 2016.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.967
And you can hear Trump
talking about

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.235
paying off a Playboy model.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.536
Yeah, it was the first time ever

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.370
that Trump didn't want
to hear himself talk.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.472
He's like, "Turn that off.
Turn it off."

00:00:40.472 --> 00:00:42.074
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:45.545
It's a big story, and CNN was
the first to release the tape.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:46.846
When he heard, Trump was like,

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.115
"Seriously, CNN, what have I
ever done to you guys?

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.984
I mean --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:53.786
I thought we --"

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:56.222
Right before the Cohen tape
was released,

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:59.425
Trump warned people not to
believe what they see or hear.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.861
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.129
Americans were like, "Trust us.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.964
We haven't believed anything
we've seen or heard

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:05.965
since election day.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.567
So we're good with that.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.835
You don't have to tell us."

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.470
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.639
But on the tape, Trump
and his lawyer Michael Cohen

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:15.341
discussed
some pretty serious issues,

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.575
though at one point,

00:01:16.575 --> 00:01:18.277
Trump seemed to have
a little trouble focusing.

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:19.345
Listen to this.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:33.359
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.861
Focus, man!

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.162
-Come on.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.896
-You know Melania
was in the next room

00:01:37.896 --> 00:01:40.232
shaking up a can of Coke,
going, "Just a second, honey.

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:41.534
Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.403
Oh, yeah, I'm going to get you
a Coke, all right."

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:48.241
It turns out that actually isn't
the only tape that exists.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.643
And I'm being told that CNN
just released another one.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.145
-Really?
-Let's take a listen.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.931
Sunny D.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.533
He wants Sunny D.

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:15.968
-Sunny D.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.504
-Hang on. I'm now hearing that
there's actually one more tape.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:20.807
-Really?
-Let's listen to this one.

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:32.685
Macaulay, that's not even close.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.320
That's not even close
to what her name is.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.590
-Wow!
Glad we got those tapes.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.025
-Some more political news.

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:42.161
I read that Vladimir Putin is
not accepting Trump's invitation

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:44.964
to visit the White House
in the fall.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:47.966
Putin was like, "Why do I need
invitation to my own home?"

00:02:47.966 --> 00:02:49.402
And you go, "Wait, wait."

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:51.104
[ Applause ]

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.571
Be careful.

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:53.806
Hey, I saw that this fall,

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:55.675
Hillary Clinton
is going to guest-star

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.077
on an episode
of "Madam Secretary."

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.878
If she becomes
a big enough TV star,

00:02:59.878 --> 00:03:02.048
she might have a chance
of becoming president.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.383
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.051
[ Applause ]

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.720
That's right.
That's right.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.589
Hillary Clinton will be
appearing on "Madam Secretary."

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:12.424
And apparently
she started a trend,

00:03:12.424 --> 00:03:13.926
'cause now a lot of politicians

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:15.995
are planning to make cameos
on TV shows.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.430
I'll show you what I mean.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.398
For instance, Jeff Sessions
is going to make an appearance

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:21.500 line:0%
on "Young Sheldon"

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.202 line:0%
as Old Young Sheldon.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:26.205 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:29.809 line:0%
Next up, Paul Ryan will be
on an episode of "Riverdale"

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.412 line:0%
as the kid who's way too old
to go to their school.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:34.847 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:38.217 line:0%
And finally, Mitch McConnell
is doing a cameo on "Franklin"

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:40.019 line:0%
as Franklin's twin brother.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.287 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:44.523
They're all doing cameos.
Very interesting.

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:46.125
Oh, I read that New Jersey

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:49.328
is suspending many of its cases
related to marijuana,

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:51.497
and people think it means
soon it will be legal.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.533
[ Cheering ]

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.335
That might explain
this welcome sign.

00:03:58.770 --> 00:03:59.839 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:02.074
"No, forget --"
"I did forget about it."

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:04.043
"Forget about what?"

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.678
And finally,
this is very interesting.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.880
Yelp is going to start showing
what restaurants scored

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.915
on their health inspections.

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:12.551
So if you want to know how
your favorite restaurant did,

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:13.786
trust me, no, you don't.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.220
We have a great show tonight.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:16.589
Give it up for the Roots.

